00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:25,520
application or on the work on made in the design phase. This is a way of parallelizing activity to

195
00:28:25,520 --> 00:28:35,440
to make more activity in the time unit and also to improve quality. It has been

196
00:28:35,440 --> 00:28:42,000
demonstrated, especially for the software development that this kind of approach, this physical approach

197
00:28:42,640 --> 00:28:47,280
can lead to a higher quality once you reach the implementation phase. For example,

198
00:28:47,280 --> 00:29:03,520
the number of bugs that a software developed with this process is 50% less than using the waterfall approach,

199
00:29:03,520 --> 00:29:08,960
so without this additional check.

200
00:29:08,960 --> 00:29:22,080
The activity can be parallelized also inside the same branch. As we said, the horizontal dimension

201
00:29:22,080 --> 00:29:30,160
can also be seen as the time and let's make an example just to make you understand how the activities

202
00:29:30,160 --> 00:29:37,120
can be parallelized. Let's assume that the width of the block of the phases are actually the time

203
00:29:37,120 --> 00:29:45,760
required to end the whole phase. As we can see, by putting in a v-shape, the projection on the time axis

204
00:29:47,040 --> 00:29:55,520
of two blocks, for example, subsystem design and component design is less than the sum of the

205
00:29:56,160 --> 00:30:02,080
singular time required for subsystem design and component design. This is because it is possible to

206
00:30:02,080 --> 00:30:09,280
do the same kind of verification, the same kind of check between these two processes. So while I'm, for

207
00:30:09,280 --> 00:30:17,040
example, in subsystem design, I can do part of the work and then give it to the component design colleagues

208
00:30:17,040 --> 00:30:26,320
that can check if they can understand it, if it's feasible, if it's consistent and so on. So they can make

209
00:30:26,320 --> 00:30:33,440
in parallel this additional check in order to save time, in order to save project time.

210
00:30:35,280 --> 00:30:43,520
A really important feature of the Divocycle is that it's completely scalable. What does it mean?

211
00:30:44,640 --> 00:30:51,760
We are now seeing the Divocycle process applied to the whole vehicle, but what about, for example,

212
00:30:51,760 --> 00:31:02,240
if we explore the subsystem design phase, I can use the Vocycle, for example, for the software of my subsystem.

213
00:31:03,680 --> 00:31:12,160
So I can adapt the phase and I will have a software requirement phase and software architecture and

214
00:31:12,160 --> 00:31:19,040
software design configuration on the design and development branch. And I will have unit testing,

215
00:31:19,040 --> 00:31:24,960
integration testing and functional testing of the whole software. The process is exactly the same,

216
00:31:24,960 --> 00:31:31,040
but it's used to develop the software. This is very important because it allows the various actors

217
00:31:31,040 --> 00:31:36,880
we've seen before, the OEM, for example, Tire 1 and Tire 2, to speak the same language when they

218
00:31:36,880 --> 00:31:43,440
interact with each other for the design and development of vehicle subsystem and components.

219
00:31:44,320 --> 00:31:50,080
They can use the same terminology, they can use the same phases, and it's very easy for them to coordinate

220
00:31:50,080 --> 00:31:54,720
between each other when they are applying the very same process, the Vocycle process.

221
00:31:56,560 --> 00:32:04,560
There are also advanced use of the Vocycle process. For example, it is possible to make iteration or to

222
00:32:04,560 --> 00:32:15,680
apply the agility concept to it. This means, for example, I can make iteration, for example, between two

223
00:32:16,480 --> 00:32:22,720
consequent phases of my process in order to improve quality. So I can reiterate the process more and

224
00:32:22,720 --> 00:32:30,080
more time on small parts of the design in order to improve the quality. And I also can do iteration

225
00:32:30,080 --> 00:32:39,840
of the quality assurance brands. For example, I can do subsystem design, integration testing, reiterating

226
00:32:39,840 --> 00:32:46,800
it, adding new functionalities to every iteration in order to keep things under control and improve

227
00:32:46,800 --> 00:32:49,520
quality. The same for component design and component testing.

228
00:32:49,520 --> 00:33:00,880
So let's make a very quick example of a running Vocycle.

229
00:33:04,240 --> 00:33:11,840
From now on, you will see on the top right of the slide the phase of the process in which we are.

230
00:33:11,840 --> 00:33:25,440
So you don't get lost with the discussion. For the example, we will imagine we want to

231
00:33:26,320 --> 00:33:36,320
introduce a new functionality in our airbag subsystem, in our vehicle. Now the airbag system is a critical

232
00:33:36,320 --> 00:33:44,960
module module of a vehicle because it has the safety of the driver and the occupant of the vehicle are

233
00:33:44,960 --> 00:33:52,000
involved. And basically, an airbag system has two requirements, two main requirements. It has to

234
00:33:52,000 --> 00:33:57,680
deploy flawlessly in case of a major accident. So it has to deploy always in case of an accident.

235
00:33:57,680 --> 00:34:04,080
But at the same time, it doesn't have to deploy, never has to deploy when it is not required because

236
00:34:04,080 --> 00:34:09,760
it is dangerous when it is deployed like that. So it is easy to understand that the

237
00:34:09,760 --> 00:34:15,440
malfunction of the airbag system shall be promptly and properly notified to the final user. The final

238
00:34:15,440 --> 00:34:25,680
user has to know when, for any reason, the airbag system of his vehicle is not functioning. So let's

239
00:34:25,680 --> 00:34:32,320
imagine we want to introduce, we want to add this notification feature to our car.

240
00:34:32,320 --> 00:34:42,560
And for example, the first thing we may be reasoning about is how I do this notification, where I put

241
00:34:42,560 --> 00:34:48,400
this notification physically inside the car. For example, the first candidate could be the

242
00:34:49,360 --> 00:34:55,760
IPC subsystem, the instrument panel cluster, which is the first thing the driver see when he's driving.

243
00:34:57,120 --> 00:35:02,000
So for example, our first requirement could be that this notification of one function can be

244
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:12,240
installed in our instrument panel cluster. Then again, we say that airbag system is involved in

245
00:35:12,240 --> 00:35:19,760
functional safety. Our team from functional safety suggests that the mechanism providing the malfunction

246
00:35:19,760 --> 00:35:26,000
notification shall be reliable. We don't want that the notification itself, it's not working for some

247
00:35:26,000 --> 00:35:43,200
reason. So they gave us a metric. For example, they can tell us, I want that the notification is 99% reliable. I want it

248
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:48,000
to be working 99% of the time. So it should be to be field proof to a certain degree. This is a second requirement at high level, a vehicle concept that we have. Another requirement is that it should be

249
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:58,240
to be field proof to be field proof to be field proof to a certain degree. This is a second requirement at high level, a vehicle concept that we have. Another example of a requirement at vehicle level,

250
00:35:58,240 --> 00:36:00,560
for example, our homologation colleagues

251
00:36:03,440 --> 00:36:07,600
inform us that there are there are constraints on how

252
00:36:07,600 --> 00:36:16,960
how the notification is given in particular they told us they tell us that a very peculiar icon must be used

253
00:36:17,680 --> 00:36:24,640
and we can choose the color between orange and red, which is red. So we have a dirt requirement. The icon shall be

254
00:36:25,280 --> 00:36:27,600
shaped like to one that is

255
00:36:29,360 --> 00:36:33,680
enforced by the homologation regulations and the color will be red.

256
00:36:33,680 --> 00:36:42,800
So the typical deliverables of the vehicle concept

257
00:36:44,800 --> 00:36:51,680
are basically specification requirements. We put the requirements in a document, in a document that can be

258
00:36:54,000 --> 00:36:57,840
managed, modified and kept and tracked

259
00:36:57,840 --> 00:37:05,840
in which we list all the desired functionalities, the definition of the vehicle mission, homologation

260
00:37:05,840 --> 00:37:10,880
constraints and so on. So it's basically a document.

261
00:37:13,280 --> 00:37:22,160
So what we do with the requirements we wrote at vehicle level, we transfer them to our system design team

262
00:37:23,120 --> 00:37:29,360
and then we start to analyze it and see what they shall do in order to satisfy those requirements.

263
00:37:30,720 --> 00:37:38,560
For example, our system design colleagues tell us that the vehicle has been designed with a domain-based

264
00:37:38,560 --> 00:37:40,080
topology. So we will have

265
00:37:42,240 --> 00:37:42,960
the ECU

266
00:37:44,800 --> 00:37:46,080
connected to each other

267
00:37:46,080 --> 00:38:01,600
and managed by a domain controller, the PWT ECU in this picture. The same for the chassis,

268
00:38:02,640 --> 00:38:04,720
the infotainment and the body, for example.

269
00:38:06,320 --> 00:38:12,320
They tell us, okay, the airbag control unit, the green one, is in the chassis domain.

270
00:38:13,040 --> 00:38:18,080
The instrument panel cluster, the red one, is in the infotainment domain. They are not in the same domain.

271
00:38:18,640 --> 00:38:19,200
We have to...

272
00:38:20,800 --> 00:38:23,200
First thing to do is to allow the communication

273
00:38:23,760 --> 00:38:25,920
of the information of the malfunction between

274
00:38:26,720 --> 00:38:29,280
the airbag control unit and the instrument panel cluster.

275
00:38:31,360 --> 00:38:36,000
So they produce the new requirements on their level

276
00:38:36,800 --> 00:38:45,360
to allow the communication between the two subsystems. It will, of course, involve also the chassis

277
00:38:45,840 --> 00:38:53,040
and the infotainment domain controllers. They will write a new protocol, a new message for the

278
00:38:53,040 --> 00:38:58,720
communication protocol that will transport the information of malfunction from the ACU

279
00:38:59,520 --> 00:39:02,000
subsystem to the IPC subsystem.

280
00:39:04,400 --> 00:39:10,320
So that the IPC, once this information is received, can turn on the lamp of the warning

281
00:39:10,880 --> 00:39:16,400
of the warning icon and warn the user that its airbag controller is malfunctioning.

282
00:39:19,280 --> 00:39:20,240
But also

283
00:39:20,240 --> 00:39:28,880
So, from the requirement at the PICOR level, we had the request that the malfunction notification

284
00:39:28,880 --> 00:39:37,840
shall be reliable, shall be very reliable. So our system engineers decide to violate locally

285
00:39:37,840 --> 00:39:48,320
the isolation of the domains by adding a direct communication between the ACU and the IPC

286
00:39:50,560 --> 00:39:57,280
in order to transport the very same information with a different medium. In this case,

287
00:39:57,280 --> 00:40:03,520
it's a simple pin-to-pin electrical communication. So when the ACU detect a malfunction, we will send

288
00:40:03,520 --> 00:40:11,360
the message on the communication bus and also will raise the voltage on this pin-to-pin communication

289
00:40:11,360 --> 00:40:18,560
in order to give the information to the IPC in two different ways. We actually

290
00:40:18,560 --> 00:40:23,680
create the redundancy in order to improve the reliability of the system.

291
00:40:25,760 --> 00:40:29,760
Okay. Typical derivables of this phase.

292
00:40:30,480 --> 00:40:36,560
It's, for example, the ACU topology, like the picture you are watching now.

293
00:40:37,280 --> 00:40:42,240
Of course, it will be more detailed, but basically how the ACU are connected between each other.

294
00:40:42,240 --> 00:40:50,320
The communication bus specification, so the list of messages that every ACU exchange with the others.

295
00:40:51,040 --> 00:40:56,960
And there may be documents, called vehicle functions, that are specification,

296
00:40:56,960 --> 00:41:04,320
specific specification, detailed on the subsystem functionalities. For example,

297
00:41:04,320 --> 00:41:10,720
there will be a document called airbag management, which explains all the functionalities that are related

298
00:41:10,720 --> 00:41:23,920
to the airbag subsystem. With these requirements at system level, we can now involve the subsystem designer,

299
00:41:23,920 --> 00:41:33,920
typically a tier one or more than one tier one, with our system requirements. For example, we will send

300
00:41:33,920 --> 00:41:42,480
the system requirements to the suppliers that provide us the airbag control unit. And we say, okay,

301
00:41:43,920 --> 00:41:49,920
these are the functionalities we want to implement. Just modify your subsystem in order to comply with it.

302
00:41:49,920 --> 00:41:57,040
The same will be done with the IPC and the Enforcement Chassis Domain Controller. So, for example, the ACU

303
00:41:57,040 --> 00:42:06,800
tier one will decide that it shall be possible by its subsystem to have diagnostic functionality implemented,

304
00:42:06,800 --> 00:42:17,360
because it has to be capable of detecting an error upon itself. For example, the software shall be capable of

305
00:42:17,360 --> 00:42:23,280
detecting if an actuator or a sensor is disconnected or it's not working,

306
00:42:23,280 --> 00:42:32,880
testing and so on. And so that the information of my function can be produced and can be put on the

307
00:42:32,880 --> 00:42:43,680
communication bus and on the dedicated pin. In a similar way, the tier one from the IPC will modify its

308
00:42:43,680 --> 00:42:49,920
subsystem in order to accept the information from the communication bus and the dedicated pin.

309
00:42:50,720 --> 00:42:58,240
the software will be modified in order to interpret this information and use to trigger the turning on of

310
00:42:58,240 --> 00:43:08,560
the lamp to get red light behind the icon on the dashboard. For the two domains controller,

311
00:43:11,040 --> 00:43:19,360
in this case, it's done what is called the gateway. So, the chassis and the infotainment will

312
00:43:19,360 --> 00:43:29,040
receive the information from the ECU in their domain and will just put it on the other communication

313
00:43:29,040 --> 00:43:35,120
channel in order to allow the switch of domain. So, to transfer the information without modification to

314
00:43:35,120 --> 00:43:46,400
the other domain. At this level, we typically have deliverables such as the hardware schematics or the

315
00:43:46,400 --> 00:43:53,120
so-called software design and software requirements specification. So, everything which is the software

316
00:43:53,120 --> 00:43:59,120
of the subsystem is produced in this phase and we also have the input output specification of the subsystems.

317
00:44:01,520 --> 00:44:06,480
Then we go at components level. The components for even for a simple application like that will be

318
00:44:06,480 --> 00:44:13,280
thousands. So, we'll just focus on the most important one, the most visible one, which is

319
00:44:13,280 --> 00:44:25,920
the red light, the red lead. And of course, the tire one that produces the IPC, it's not also a producer of lead,

320
00:44:25,920 --> 00:44:34,240
a manufacturer of lead. So, they will call a tire two specialized in building of lead light.

321
00:44:34,240 --> 00:44:45,520
They will ask for a red lead. And the tire two will provide, for example, a catalog of or a spreadsheet of

322
00:44:46,160 --> 00:44:54,720
possible candidates. The tire one can choose the one that is more appropriate for the application and it

323
00:44:54,720 --> 00:45:07,360
will install it in the subsystem. This is the usual way to interact with tire two. So, you don't develop a new lead

324
00:45:07,360 --> 00:45:16,080
for the application, but you just choose an already existing lead, which is a good match for your application.

325
00:45:16,080 --> 00:45:26,960
And then we have all the components. We have designed the subsystems and non-vehicle concept. We are done. So, we can implement

326
00:45:27,600 --> 00:45:38,800
all the modification and we will start to test it. Of course, you start testing at component level. So, the lower level. But

327
00:45:38,800 --> 00:45:51,600
let me ask you something. It is possible, for example, do you believe it's possible to test

328
00:45:52,160 --> 00:45:57,520
the lead before it's actually installed in the vehicle? The answer is, of course, yes. You can

329
00:45:57,520 --> 00:46:06,160
parallelize the activity testing and, for example, you can use a little bench with just minimal electronics

330
00:46:06,160 --> 00:46:15,840
in order to test if the lead does turn on when the current is applied or not. So, you don't have

331
00:46:15,840 --> 00:46:22,240
actually to wait for the whole implementation to test it. This is another way in which you can

332
00:46:22,240 --> 00:46:28,400
parallelize activities in the vehicle. Basically, for the component testing, but this is also applicable

333
00:46:28,400 --> 00:46:39,120
for every kind of testing. The testing activity itself is basically making the right questions and

334
00:46:39,120 --> 00:46:46,480
providing the answer. For the lead, for example, the question can be, does the lead turn when powered?

335
00:46:47,200 --> 00:46:57,680
The components work as it is intended to do? The answer to this question is the test result. So, you do the

336
00:46:57,680 --> 00:47:04,240
test and you check it. Yes or no. It does work or it does not work. If it does not work, let's see

337
00:47:04,240 --> 00:47:13,040
what the problem is. Typical unit tests. So, typical test component level are, for example, a simple piece

338
00:47:13,040 --> 00:47:20,640
of electronics like the lead or capacitor or so on. The testing of a single software module or portion of

339
00:47:20,640 --> 00:47:28,240
software, the testing of electrical harness and so on. The main deliverable of every testing phase,

340
00:47:28,880 --> 00:47:34,640
it's the test result document. So, a list of tests with the result of the test that you can share

341
00:47:35,840 --> 00:47:44,320
with whom may be interested in the test result. Same approach with the integration test at subsystem level. So,

342
00:47:44,320 --> 00:47:53,600
also, you introduce the modification to all the subsystems and you start testing the single subsystem

343
00:47:53,600 --> 00:48:00,160
without putting it in a vehicle. This is also can be done without a full integration in the vehicle. So, you don't

344
00:48:00,160 --> 00:48:09,680
need a fully implemented vehicle to test at this level. You just need to, for example, use an hardware in the loop,

345
00:48:09,680 --> 00:48:18,720
a simulator in which you just connect your single subsystem to see if it does react correctly to the

346
00:48:18,720 --> 00:48:27,360
stimulation from the outside. For example, you can test your air brake control unit at another in the loop

347
00:48:27,360 --> 00:48:35,040
bench. You can, for example, disconnect manually a sensor and test if the software detect it and raise an

348
00:48:35,040 --> 00:48:45,040
error. You can test if, after an error is raised, the information is properly communicated through

349
00:48:45,600 --> 00:48:54,960
the communication bus and dedicated pin and so on. The same can be done for the testing on the IPC subsystem

350
00:48:54,960 --> 00:49:00,560
and infotainment HSC domain controllers. So, you can just test the single subsystem without putting in the

351
00:49:00,560 --> 00:49:10,080
vehicle. The same deliverable is present here as any test phase. So, the integration test result document

352
00:49:10,720 --> 00:49:18,320
but also, usually in this phase, there can be another output, another result which is

353
00:49:19,840 --> 00:49:26,880
commonly called a change request. What is the change request? Imagine the case that you are testing your

354
00:49:26,880 --> 00:49:36,880
subsystem, you discover that actually the implementation is compliant to the requirement. So, it is correct

355
00:49:37,840 --> 00:49:44,240
by a formal point of view, but the behavior, the final behavior, the physical behavior of the subsystem

356
00:49:44,960 --> 00:49:54,160
is not compliant to what it shall be the mission or the expected behavior of the component. In this case,

357
00:49:54,160 --> 00:50:07,120
you highlight this problem by doing a change request. So, you go back to your design colleagues and say,

358
00:50:07,120 --> 00:50:13,680
okay, this is implemented as the requirement says, but maybe it's the requirement itself that is

359
00:50:15,840 --> 00:50:22,560
that is wrong or that is not detailed enough, that is not 100% correct. So, we have to change it,

360
00:50:22,560 --> 00:50:29,120
we have to modify it. So, you actually go back, you go back to the left branch, you modify the requirements

361
00:50:29,120 --> 00:50:36,480
and do another time the cycle in order to see if you corrected the problem.

362
00:50:39,840 --> 00:50:48,240
Same goes for the test at vehicle level, so for the functional tests. In this case, we will actually

363
00:50:48,240 --> 00:50:55,360
implement everything in a vehicle. Usually, in this phase, at the end, a vehicle is required we don't

364
00:50:55,360 --> 00:51:03,600
implement. You do the functionality test, the acceptance test, and for example, you will

365
00:51:05,520 --> 00:51:14,240
analyze things like, okay, I'm setting the car. There is a malfunction. Do I see the icon? The icon

366
00:51:14,240 --> 00:51:19,600
it's evident, it's visible, the color is the right one, the shape is the right one, and so on.

367
00:51:20,400 --> 00:51:27,040
So, the final implementation does satisfy my original requirements at vehicle level.

368
00:51:28,720 --> 00:51:35,280
And again, you will have an integration test result document for this phase, and

369
00:51:35,280 --> 00:51:42,880
if required, a change request if some other problem is detected at this level.

370
00:51:45,920 --> 00:51:54,880
Okay, this was the collection on the cycle. Those are my contacts. If you want to have

